{"id": "EUVD-2026-103771", "enisaUuid": "516432ec-6f50-34eb-a3ec-031bb7d8a2c8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nof/overlay: don't leak fragment references when changeset init fails\n\ninit_overlay_changeset() stores the number of initialized fragments\nin ovcs->count only on full success. When find_target() or the\n__symbols__ lookup fails partway through, the target and overlay\nreferences taken for the fragments initialized so far are never\ndropped: free_overlay_changeset() bounds its cleanup loop by\novcs->count, which is still 0.\n\nStore the running count on the error path so free_overlay_changeset()\nputs whatever was set up. The store is guarded by ovcs->fragments\nbecause on the allocation-failure path cnt still holds the counting\npass total while there is no fragments array; everywhere else cnt\nonly counts fully-initialized fragments.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:49:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:57:18", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/702b5db6e7b3865be70675d57d6fd7dde80d02b6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/894573e2fdaeb1b15030b7eebc22615edf28a6cd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7a46f1917b320cc8762183b802301da02a191b6a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3a23fb158ba517b77a2e5258263bdfdaa480f758", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1d62f0f2bc7edb12ed09f71203df0e47fa4efca4"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98831", "GHSA-vvrp-cfq6-9c5c"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "50e82bd4-2ad2-3118-8029-2ed8d24876e0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "61b4de4e0b384f4a22c55c3bada604da49cec4e1 <3a23fb158ba517b77a2e5258263bdfdaa480f758"}, {"id": "64d9d00e-38e5-3dab-bfdc-ba039d1fc1bf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6b4efac8-058e-31a7-a585-45d8c2d54b47", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "a05a6d54-a904-36e2-8357-70402fc9394f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.15"}, {"id": "a1ef07c9-c315-3ef0-930e-5f96e187238c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "a6244f0d-8607-3ee8-b2ca-9c1d1dfbc0a2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "b7f02ae3-ca5c-3b03-9d0f-d48408ed54dd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "61b4de4e0b384f4a22c55c3bada604da49cec4e1 <1d62f0f2bc7edb12ed09f71203df0e47fa4efca4"}, {"id": "bb785855-dfba-325b-9ae1-d92dc629071b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "61b4de4e0b384f4a22c55c3bada604da49cec4e1 <702b5db6e7b3865be70675d57d6fd7dde80d02b6"}, {"id": "cd89ce38-2111-3819-86ad-8ca9b9e481bb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "ce391c92-420e-3822-9a66-bba36c8435ea", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "61b4de4e0b384f4a22c55c3bada604da49cec4e1 <7a46f1917b320cc8762183b802301da02a191b6a"}, {"id": "f69df86a-af82-372b-b2f9-bb28303663d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "61b4de4e0b384f4a22c55c3bada604da49cec4e1 <894573e2fdaeb1b15030b7eebc22615edf28a6cd"}, {"id": "fa0a0ff0-b92d-3cd4-903b-5be1e18aefd3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "48cfcbe8-63c2-3bce-a8ce-d114e50774da", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}